* '''Precedent:''' this page is deliberately short. The conflation algorithm, review UI, check suite, audit log and revert plan are '''the same machinery''', unchanged, as [[Toronto/Import/AddressPoints]] — reviewed by the community in May 2026 and used for 1,297 production changesets. That page is the long-form reference; this one records only what is different about Guelph.

== Credit where it is due ==

Guelph's civic addresses were '''already imported''', solo, by [https://www.openstreetmap.org/user/ARandomThumbtack_Import ARandomThumbtack_Import] between 2025-09-16 and 2025-10-23, from the same City of Guelph open dataset, documented at [[Guelph/Address_Import]] and finished ahead of their own self-imposed deadline. It is careful, well-tagged work: the changesets carry <code>import=yes</code>, <code>import:page</code>, <code>source</code> and <code>source:license</code>, which is more than most bulk address edits in Ontario manage, and it is the reason Guelph is one of only two municipalities in a 42-dataset Ontario survey with address coverage above 90%.

'''Thank you.''' This proposal exists because that import worked, not because it did not. Nothing here revisits, re-imports or supersedes it — [[Guelph/Address_Import]] remains the record of the original import and belongs to its author. What follows is maintenance layered on top of finished work.

ARandomThumbtack was contacted before this page was written and is content for the maintainer to take on continuous upkeep; they are invited onto the reviewer roster below, and they retain a standing veto over anything touching Guelph addresses.

== What is proposed ==

'''Continuous''', human-reviewed gap-fill of the civic addresses the City publishes and OSM does not yet have, re-run each time the City's dataset changes — plus the QA findings that fall out of running conflation over a city that is already mapped.

That is the difference from Toronto, and it is the whole point of this page:

* Toronto was a '''one-time''' import of half a million missing addresses into a city that had almost none.
* Guelph is '''already complete'''. The valuable product is not an initial upload; it is staying in sync with the City afterwards, which is what nobody is signed up to do today.

=== Scope ===

Measured against source snapshot 39 (2026-08-13): 53,846 active source rows, collapsing to '''40,634 civic addresses'''.

{| class="wikitable"
! Item !! Figure !! Disposition
|-
| Civic addresses missing from OSM || '''2,523''' of 40,634 (6.2%) || Candidates for upload; hand-measured via Overpass, 2026-08-10. Diffuse — there is no unmapped district. These are the tail the original import parked in <code>RemainingAddresses.osm</code>, plus everything the City has published since October 2025.
|-
| New addresses per City update || small, unknown || The recurring workload this proposal is actually about. Tracked snapshot-to-snapshot by <code>ontario-address-changes</code>.
|-
| Unit-level addresses || 13,162 source unit rows || '''Out of scope.''' Source rows are collapsed to one candidate per civic address (<code>[units] policy = "collapse-to-civic"</code>). Guelph's units are largely ''already in OSM'' — 5,422 objects carry the unit twice, as <code>addr:housenumber=714-30</code> ''and'' <code>addr:unit=30</code>. Normalising that is a separate mechanical edit under the [[Automated Edits code of conduct]], not consensual yet, and not part of this proposal. Nothing here re-tags an existing node.
|-
| Street-name disagreements || to be reported || Output of the <code>nearby_street_mismatch</code> check. Reported, never auto-corrected.
|-
| OSM-only addresses || to be reported || Addresses OSM has and the City source does not. '''Never deleted''' — see non-goals.
|}

=== Goals ===

* Keep OSM's Guelph civic-address coverage current against the City's roster, continuously, rather than as a one-off.
* Surface disagreements between OSM and the City source — street names, positions, duplicates — to local mappers as reviewable findings.
* Preserve a per-candidate audit trail (source row → verdict → reviewer decision → changeset id → resulting OSM id), as in Toronto.

=== Non-goals ===

Identical to [[Toronto/Import/AddressPoints#Goals and non-goals|§ Non-goals of the Toronto import]], and they carry extra weight here because this city is somebody else's finished work:

* '''No deletions''', including addresses the City source no longer lists.
* '''No mutation of existing OSM objects''' — this creates new nodes only. In particular, no re-tagging of the 2025 import's nodes.
* '''No unit-level import''', no <code>addr:interpolation</code> cleanup, no polygons, no geometry editing.

== Import data ==

* '''Dataset:''' City of Guelph address points, [https://explore.guelph.ca/datasets/cityofguelph::addresses-1/explore explore.guelph.ca] — the same dataset the 2025 import used.
* '''Licence:''' OGL-Canada-2.0, as recorded by the prior import. ODbL-compatible: permissive attribution, no share-alike, no non-commercial clause. Attribution is satisfied by the <code>source</code> tag on the node and on the containing changeset.
* '''Consumption path:''' the City feed is snapshotted into SQLite by [https://github.com/skfd/ontario-address-changes ontario-address-changes], which diffs consecutive snapshots. That diff is what makes "continuous" cheap — each cycle re-conflates the whole city, but the review queue is normally only what changed.
* '''OSM side:''' Geofabrik Ontario PBF, re-pulled before each cycle. If more than 24 h elapse between conflation and upload, re-fetch and re-conflate.
* '''Review partition:''' the City's 23 "Guelph Areas" community polygons (<code>AREA_NAME</code>), covering 99.47% of source points. The 287 orphans are city-edge cases plus the 75 <code>Guelph/Eramosa Twp</code> rows, which lie outside the city fabric by construction and are held back — see § Open questions.

== Tagging plan ==

Only the '''deltas''' from [[Toronto/Import/AddressPoints#Tagging plan|§ Tagging plan of the Toronto import]] are listed. All uploaded elements are nodes; no ways, no relations.

{| class="wikitable"
! Tag !! Value !! Note
|-
| <code>addr:housenumber</code> || source <code>STREETNO</code> || As Toronto.
|-
| <code>addr:street</code> || source <code>FULLNAME</code> || Already in OSM long form ("Cork Street West") on 100% of rows — the suffix-expansion step Toronto needed is a no-op here.
|-
| <code>addr:city</code> || <code>Guelph</code> || '''Delta from Toronto''', which omits <code>addr:city</code>. Emitted here to stay consistent with the 2025 import, which wrote it on every node.
|-
| <code>addr:province</code> || <code>Ontario</code> || '''Delta from Toronto''', which omits province per Canadian convention. Written by the 2025 import and dominant in Guelph's OSM data today (3,699 <code>Ontario</code> against 178 <code>ON</code> in the sampled elements). See § Open questions.
|-
| <code>addr:postcode</code> || enrichment only || Written only when a same-address POI already in OSM carries one. Never invented, never extrapolated.
|-
| <code>source</code> || <code>City of Guelph Open Data</code> || On the node and on the changeset.
|}

Deliberately '''not''' emitted: <code>addr:unit</code> (see scope), <code>addr:ward</code> (the source's 1–6 ward integer is modelled better as an admin polygon), <code>addr:housename</code>, <code>addr:country</code>, and any city-specific custom namespace.

