== Revert plan ==

As [[Toronto/Import/AddressPoints#Revert plan|§ Revert plan of the Toronto import]]. Every upload is a distinct changeset from a dedicated account, with a per-run manifest of <code>(source_id, address, osm_node_id, changeset_id)</code>, so any batch can be reverted in isolation without touching neighbouring work. Because this import creates nodes only and never modifies existing objects, a revert cannot damage the 2025 import or any organic mapping.

== Open questions for the community ==

# '''<code>addr:province=Ontario</code>.''' The 2025 import wrote it as a constant; the Toronto import omits province per Canadian convention; Guelph's OSM data is now overwhelmingly tagged with it. Local consistency and provincial convention point in opposite directions. The current plan is to follow local consistency and keep writing it — objections welcome, and this is the single tagging decision most worth arguing about.
# '''The 75 <code>Guelph/Eramosa Twp</code> rows.''' The City publishes them past its own boundary, and Wellington County publishes the same addresses. Held back until someone says which source should own them.
# '''Unit normalisation.''' Separate from this proposal, and unresolved: 5,422 objects double-encode the unit (<code>addr:housenumber=714-30</code> plus <code>addr:unit=30</code>, in an order that is not even the Canada Post one). The maintainer and the original importer disagree; testing against Nominatim on 2026-08-21 showed unit-level search does not work under ''any'' tagging scheme, which removes searchability as an argument either way. Being argued on [https://community.openstreetmap.org/t/import-addresses-from-city-of-guelph-data/135103 thread #135103].
# '''Cadence and quiet.''' How often should a maintenance batch be announced on the forum thread: every batch, or a periodic summary?

